TEXT -640 -440 Left 3 ;BASELINE - Rev B POWER BOARD AS BUILT (Nov 2024) - why it cannot reach its own full scale
TEXT -640 -400 Left 1 ;One of the two identical channels.  U3 = LMV358 powered from +4.096 V (REF5040) -> gate can never exceed ~4.1 V.\nIRF530 VGS(th) is 2-4 V (datasheet) and the 0.1 R source resistor needs another 0.3-0.6 V, so the\nreachable current depends on which IRF530 you got.  Op-amp = ideal rail-to-rail proxy (best case for LMV358).
TEXT 240 400 Left 1 ;VSEN amplifier as drawn: R1 (feedback) goes to the\nNON-inverting input and R4 to the inverting input.\nPositive feedback -> output latches to a rail.\nCorrect: swap the R1 and R4 connections.
TEXT -640 720 Left 2 !.param Vdut=12 vth=3\n.model IRF530_VTH VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto={vth} Rd=50m Rs=12m Rb=60m Kp=5 lambda=.01 Cgdmax=1n Cgdmin=.26n Cgs=.2n Cjo=.4n Is=52p ksubthres=.1 Vds=100)\n.step param vth list 2 3 4   ; IRF530 VGS(th) min / mid / max\n.dc Vctrl 0 4.096 8m\n.meas DC I_FS FIND Id(Q1) AT 4.096\n.meas DC I_target PARAM 4.096*12/80/0.1\n.meas DC Vgate_FS FIND V(gate) AT 4.096\n.meas DC VSEN_out FIND V(VSEN) AT 2\n.meas DC VSEN_correct PARAM 0.1*12
